  "caption": "Quinn's new motto: more is more. By week five, Quinn was slower, grumpier and lying awake at 3am, so naturally… trained harder.\n\nYour body adapts during recovery, not just during effort. And work, family and life stress draw from the same recovery budget as training.\n\nWhat often helps: drop to easy activity for one to three weeks, protect your sleep and eat enough, then return with easy days and a lighter week every third or fourth week. Count life stress as training stress, and track resting heart rate, sleep and mood.\n\nIf fatigue lasts for weeks even with rest, or you notice changes in your cycle, appetite or weight, see your GP.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
